PETSELFTEST1
# V9 1E (G4): the spoken rule of a play game. Memory4 (card 8) is entered
# and left alone: the rule is asked when it opens and once more after 12 s
# without input (real time, 13 s wait). Needs no recording: take
# /sounds/default.kps off the card, or this expects PET_GAME_RULE_PACK
# instead of _TONE (the tone is the fallback). Quiet hours refuse games,
# so the day phase is pinned. The menu steps follow v8_play_games (1A).
# Counted from "mark begin" (see tools/selftest_report.py).
# expect min:PET_GAME_RULE_TONE 2
# expect none:PET_GAME_RULE_PACK 0
# expect min:game=memory4 1
# expect min:end=home 1
# expect none:PET_GAME_REFUSED 0
# expect none:PET_GAME_START_FAILED 0
# expect none:PET_SLEEP_REQUESTED 0
# expect none:PET_SELFTEST_ABORT 0
# expect selftest_done 1
# expect max_partial_ms 2500
# expect max_full_ms 5000
phase day
volume 15
waitidle 60000
pet
wait 6000
# Normalize restored pet state to "home, neutral".
tap press 6000
hold press 1500 6000
mark begin
# Rail Story(1) -> Game(2), press: play menu.
tap down 2500
tap press 6000
# V9 1A: Brain page (card 1), memory4 is its 4th card.
tap down 600
tap press 3000
tap down 600
tap down 600
tap down 600
tap press 6000
# Nobody plays: the rule at the start, again after 12 s (real time).
wait 13000
hold press 1500 8000
pet
wait 5000
end
